WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.470
So this is Slifer the Sky Dragon!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.970
Look.  These five cards form the ultimate combo, God Five!

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.570
Flawless and invincible.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.730
This God formation is unbeatable!

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.720
I can't win.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.600
There's no way to defeat Slifer.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:55.040
Get up, Yugi!

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:00.730
If a God stands in your way, knock God down!

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:06.740
Surpass God!
Ultimate Infinite Loop

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.550
Get up, Yugi!

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.620
Understood, Kaiba!

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.500
Just wait!

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.040
I'll now defeat a God!

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.450
How convenient.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.600
Seto Kaiba, the one who has the final God Card Obelisk, has shown up.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.780
After I kill Yugi, you're next.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.230
I'm the one who will defeat Yugi.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.150
Here I go!  My turn!

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.420
I have three cards in my hand.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.020
Alpha The Magnet Warrior, Berfomet and Big Shield Gardna.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:03.960
But these three monsters are no match for Slifer's attack points.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.550
I draw.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.750
Monster Reborn.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.640
I set a card this turn.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.060
And Big Shield Gardna in defense position.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.490
When you summon a monster, Slifer's effect activates.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.120
Lightning Bullet!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:41.100
When you summon a monster, Slifer deals it 2000 points of damage.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.820
2000 points of damage?

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.220
That's a terrifying effect.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:52.000
Most monsters will be destroyed the instant that they're summoned.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:58.280
Similar to my Obelisk, when Slifer the Sky Dragon is summoned...

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.490
...it instantly destroys the opponent's spirit and chance of winning.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:03.920
Big brother!

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.320
Yugi's monster is alive!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.820
I survived, but that's not enough to win.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:19.300
Big Shield Gardna will definitely be destroyed next turn, and I'll have no monsters on my field.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:26.250
If I have no monsters, Slifer will attack me directly, and I'll lose.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.750
Is there really no way to defeat a God?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.360
Yes, keep struggling in despair.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.190
You'll grovel before me.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.140
My turn.  I draw.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:48.740
Lightforce Sword's effect ends, so I'll have 11 cards in my hand.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:52.500
Slifer now has 11,000 attack points.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.340
11,000!

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:05.280
Big brother, that monster gains attack points for every card in his hand.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.020
That's not all.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:12.460
Due to Infinite Cards, his hand no longer has an upper limit.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.960
What?  He can raise its attack points forever?

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.740
Is there a way to beat such a monster?

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.450
Infinite attack points...

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.050
Infinite...

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:27.900
Infinite?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.680
I got it!

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.620
God is using infinity to trick us.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.050
Yugi, I know how to beat a God.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.490
Here I go.  Slifer attacks.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:44.290
Destroy Big Shield Gardna!

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.330
If you break, you're no longer a worthy opponent.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:56.030
Turn tail and run.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.770
I'll defeat him and acquire Slifer.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.070
See that?

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.210
God's power is infinite!

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.900
As his hand grows, God's power rises forever.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.160
There's no way to defeat that-

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.320
Forever?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.360
I see!

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.290
I know how to defeat the God!

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.000
He figured it out.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:18.920
Yugi!

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.760
Defeat it?

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:21.770
Yeah.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.800
It'll all be over next turn.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.700
The one left standing after that turn is the winner!

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.050
Have you lost your mind?

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.340
You think you can defeat me in one turn?

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.370
Yes!

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:43.620
Impossible!  There's no way he can make a comeback!

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.220
He's bluffing.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.200
But why is he so confident?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:02.370
If he doesn't destroy Slifer and its 11,000 attack points, he can't reduce his opponent's life points to 0.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:05.240
That's impossible to do.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:06.670
Brother.

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:08.170
Don't say anything, Mokuba.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:12.610
Watch what a true duelist can do.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.530
What a true duelist can do?

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.400
Here I go!

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:31.830
My final turn!

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:38.550
Everything depends on whether I can draw the single key card in my deck.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.960
I draw!

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.620
I win.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:51.880
What?

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:54.680
He drew the key card.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:01.060
A God Card chooses which noble duelist will become its owner.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:04.360
Here I go!  I flip over my set card!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.500
Monster Reborn!

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.430
Monster Reborn?

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:12.800
I use this card to resurrect a monster from the graveyard.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:19.460
The dragonslayer Buster Blader returns to my field!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:32.630
Your strategy is to resurrect a monster in defense position to protect your life points.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.630
That won't lead you to victory.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.100
Defense position?

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.360
You're wrong, Marik.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.800
Buster Blader in attack position!

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.210
What?  Attack position?

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.480
You're going to attack Slifer?

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:58.910
Since Slifer has 11,000 attack points, you know you'll lose all your life points.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:02.300
Marik, I have the key card in my hand.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.360
It'll create an infinite combo that surpasses your God's ultimate combo.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.290
Infinite combo?

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.240
Surpass my ultimate combo?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.300
Have you lost it?

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:19.040
There's no infinite power that's greater than God!

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:24.170
Look at my field for proof.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:30.560
The Continuous Spell Card of Safe Return's effect covers the entire field.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:37.720
If either of us resurrects a monster, I can draw three cards from my deck.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:41.660
I just resurrected Buster Blader from my graveyard.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.800
Yes.  So I draw three cards.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.330
And...

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.710
14,000 attack points!

00:09:57.050 --> 00:10:03.700
And by summoning Buster Blader, Slifer's effect activates!

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.150
Lightning Bullet!

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.150
Hang in there, Buster Blader!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:17.570
You have 3100 attack points.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:20.550
2000 points of damage won't destroy you.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:32.350
It managed to survive, but Buster Blader drops to 1100 attack points.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:35.650
Are you still planning to attack Slifer?

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.200
It's not too late.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.080
I'll let you switch it to defense position.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:45.020
Buster Blader remains in attack position, Marik!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.290
What's he thinking?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:56.430
Marik, I'll show you the infinite combo that surpasses God's ultimate combo!

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:14.820
Marik, I'll show you the infinite combo that surpasses God's ultimate combo!

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:20.820
I don't know how Yugi can still win.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:26.560
Break the illusion that God's power is infinite, Yugi!

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.000
Here I go!  It's my Battle Phase!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.940
Attack me!  You'll be the one to fall!

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:34.880
This turn will decide the duel.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.660
Buster Blader, attack Slifer the Sky Dragon!

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.640
Dragon Buster Blade!

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:49.080
I don't know what you're up to, but that monster can't touch a God.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:55.500
The Continuous Trap Jam Defender activates!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.540
Revival Jam, protect God!

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:10.050
If the attack reached Slifer, its counterattack would've destroyed Buster Blader.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:16.940
I won't let you lay a single finger on Slifer.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.600
You'll lose without being able to do anything!

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:29.320
I knew Revival Jam would protect Slifer.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:30.330
And...

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.660
I was waiting for this moment.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.300
This is my trump card!

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:42.460
The spell card Brain Control!

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.060
Brain Control?

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:54.350
It brainwashes your opponent's monster, allowing you to control it for one turn.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.600
I see.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:05.120
Too bad, but a God can't be brainwashed.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:10.480
Slifer counterattacks Buster Blader, and I win!

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.200
Wait, Marik.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:19.480
I didn't say I was brainwashing Slifer.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.610
What?

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.400
You have the wrong idea.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.050
I brainwashed Revival Jam!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.860
I summon it on my field!

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.790
What?  You brainwashed Revival Jam?

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.200
A monster has resurrected, Marik.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:46.460
Due to the Continuous Spell Card of Safe Return, draw three cards from your deck.

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:48.880
I know you're up to something.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:55.440
But thanks for raising Slifer's attack points.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:08.820
You fool.  Slifer now has 17,000 attack points.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:10.440
Counterattack, Slifer!

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.720
Finish the nameless Pharaoh!

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:14.920
Hold up.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:22.040
Before Slifer attacked me, Revival Jam resurrected on my field.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:30.280
So Slifer uses its effect on Revival Jam.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.950
What happens next?

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:41.660
Revival Jam resurrects again.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:51.230
Since a monster resurrected, you draw three cards.

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:56.680
Oh no!

00:14:56.680 --> 00:15:01.420
Slifer's effect will activate again and destroy Revival Jam.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:10.330
Then it'll resurrect, force me to draw three cards, and Slifer will attack again!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.970
This will repeat forever.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.990
It's an infinite loop!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:35.940
I can't believe it.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:40.780
If you can't draw a card from your deck, you can't continue the game.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:54.220
Marik, you said that as your hand grows forever, so would Slifer's attack points.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.230
That is incorrect.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.680
God's power isn't infinite!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.720
The number of cards in your deck limits its power!

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.060
I win, Marik!

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:32.000
Damn!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.940
I can't believe I lost!

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.580
All right!  Yugi won!

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.230
Hand over your rare card and Puzzle Card.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.820
Hey!  Hello?

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.670
He's not moving, just like a puppet.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:12.980
He must be in shock for losing like that.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.550
This is Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.150
The second God Card.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:28.200
Due to the ante rule, you get Slifer the Sky Dragon because you won.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.720
And a Puzzle Card too.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:40.700
But that Slifer card will belong to my brother soon.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.580
So this is a God Card...

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:45.300
Yugi.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.710
You have been chosen to wield the God Card.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:54.380
I'm not satisfied unless my enemies are powerful.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:55.800
Kaiba...

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:59.850
Or else, there's no point in defeating you.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:04.020
Is my brother challenging Yugi to a duel right here?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:11.970
Yugi, you know that when two duelists meet in Battle City, that location becomes the battlefield.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:14.200
Let's duel, Yugi!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.570
I should be fighting the Ghouls, not Kaiba.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.870
But do I have to accept?

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:26.250
Yugi.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:30.700
You still don't want to let the God Card go?

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:32.750
You don't know when to give up, Marik.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:38.080
Whatever.  The God Card will return to me soon enough.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.730
I'm not too worried.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:44.560
But I forgot to mention one thing.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:48.000
I'm arriving in Domino City soon.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:52.440
To fulfill a plan that I've been working on.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.250
Plan?

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:57.380
I can see three things simultaneously.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:03.530
The first is you, through the eyes of this puppet.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:07.790
The second is Domino City.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:11.520
And the last is the crowds in the city.

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:15.130
Through the eyes of the Rare Hunters in Domino City.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:21.300
Damn!  I was this close to beating Kaiba!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:25.240
You say that, but you're actually relieved.

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.750
Say what, Anzu?

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.600
I was right.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.270
I see your friends.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.380
A duelist named Jonouchi and several others.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:38.820
Jonouchi!  Everyone!

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:45.200
I can easily get the God Card back if I involve your friends.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:50.140
The Ghouls' Rare Hunters have been watching your friends all this time.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:52.630
I can use them anytime I want.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.170
That's dirty, Marik!

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.240
It's your fault.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:02.660
If you lost, your friends wouldn't be in danger.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.140
I won't forgive you!

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:09.110
I'm the one who won't forgive you.

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:13.590
My family's agony was much worse than this.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:21.880
Yugi, you better go to your friends before something tragic happens to them.

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.100
Marik!

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:26.870
Jonouchi!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.900
You're running away, Yugi?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.240
Kaiba, I can't duel you at this moment.

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.610
The Ghouls are after Jonouchi!

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:41.310
I can't forsake my friends!

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:44.780
Yugi.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.850
He chooses his friends over pride.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:59.180
I'll get Slifer the Sky Dragon back soon.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:05.270
By using my Millennium Rod to turn your friends into my pawns.

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:13.980
Jonouchi, where are you?

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.970
My deck with the god of death and destruction, The Winged Dragon of Ra...

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.000
Give me the power of the Pharaoh!

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:48.600
The two Rare Hunters blocking Yugi's way challenge him to a tag duel.

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:52.220
What?  Kaiba wants to form a tag team with Yugi?

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.880
Meanwhile, we're unaware that Marik is after us.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:22:00.060
As we search for Jonouchi's next opponent, we run into Ryota Kajiki at the aquarium.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.400
Jonouchi, I think he's a suitable opponent!

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:07.930
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Unseen Foe
Sea Stealth II

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:09.520
Duel, standby!

00:22:23.630 --> 00:22:28.140
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:33.510
I feel like I've been here

00:22:34.030 --> 00:22:43.160
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:54.670
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:57.560 --> 00:23:02.200
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:07.470
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:12.580
Will never change

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:17.850
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:23.060
To be who I am

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:28.290
I've kept searching for something

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:33.000
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:35.940
I learned that's the answer

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:43.040
From now until forever...
